# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Full-size photo originals pulled off Instagram, kept locally so the published
# set can be re-picked without repeating the harvest (see .claude/photo-sources.md).
# Too large to commit; only the re-encoded public/photos/ frames ship.
/instagram-originals/

# NEVER COMMIT THESE. The `origin` remote (github.com/najathakram/najathakram.info)
# is PUBLIC, and both directories below contain material that must not be.
#
# /Visa/     scanned passports and visa application forms for named family
#            members. Committing this would publish other people's identity
#            documents on the open internet. Verified 2026-08-11 as never having
#            been committed in any branch; keep it that way.
# /Resume/   resume source documents and PROJECTS.md, which describes internal
#            employer work in detail. The entire point of this site's editing
#            rules is that this material stays off the public record. The two
#            resume PDFs that are MEANT to be public live in public/resume/.
/Visa/
/Resume/

# Also public-repo unsafe, for the same reason. These working documents quote the
# internal detail the site itself deliberately omits: named interop partners,
# the CFR deliverable, and unpublished measurement figures. Scanned 2026-08-11.
# `.claude/code-map/`, `review-panel.md` and `photo-sources.md` are safe and DO
# ship, since they describe the site rather than the employer's work.
/.claude/panel-reviews/
/.claude/pipeline/

.vercel
